---
const specs: [string, string][] = [
  ['Processor', 'nRF52840 (Seeed XIAO nRF52840 Plus)'],
  ['Connection', 'Bluetooth Low Energy'],
  ['CO₂, temperature, humidity', 'Sensirion SCD41'],
  ['Light', 'VEML7700'],
  ['Noise', 'SPH0641 MEMS microphone, A-weighted'],
  ['Display', '1.54″ e-ink, 152 × 152'],
  ['Storage', '64 Mb SPI flash'],
  ['Power', 'Rechargeable LiPo, deep sleep between samples'],
  ['Sampling', '10 s to 10 min, default 60 s'],
  ['Licence', 'GPLv3'],
];
---

<section id="open">
  <div class="head">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Open source</p>
      <h2>Yours to open, reflash and change</h2>
    </div>
    <p>
      Hardware, firmware and app live in one repository under GPLv3. The unit runs the Arduino bootloader, so you can
      change the firmware from the Arduino IDE and flash it over USB.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="open">
    <div class="body">
      <p>
        Temperature and humidity come from the SCD41, the same sensor that measures CO₂, instead of a board sensor that
        warms itself up. There is no VOC sensor: it draws too much current for a battery device and its number is hard
        to act on.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each sample wakes the sensors in turn, takes a burst of readings and filters it into one value with an error
        estimate, so a reading far from the trend can be dropped. Between samples the unit sleeps.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        I own an Airvalent and a couple of Xiaomi sensors, and I felt these little devices could do more. I wanted data
        you can act on: high CO₂, open a window; too much light, use a sleep mask; too much noise, try earplugs.
        <cite>From the maker, who started Quiesco in 2026</cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
    <div class="specs-wrap">
      <table>
        <tbody>
          {
            specs.map(([k, v]) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{k}</th>
                <td>{v}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .open {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 56px;
  }
  .body p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .body p + p {
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  blockquote {
    margin: 28px 0 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--drift);
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  cite {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-family: var(--text);
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .specs-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 11px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  th {
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--muted);
    width: 38%;
    padding-right: 16px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .open {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
